# Cloudflare Pages routing. The public site is the app; everything else in
# this repository is workshop material and must not be reachable from the
# open internet.
#
# There is no build step (architecture rule), so the whole repo is what gets
# uploaded — plans, tools, tests, review sheets and all. This file is the only
# place that can take them back off the public site. Pages applies these rules
# "regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming request", so a
# rule here beats the file sitting on disk.
#
# Why they point at /nowhere rather than saying "404": Pages only accepts the
# redirect status codes (301, 302, 303, 307, 308) in the third column — a
# literal 404 rule is rejected and the whole file can fail to apply. Sending
# these addresses somewhere that genuinely does not exist gets the real thing
# instead: Cloudflare answers /nowhere with a true 404 and the site's own
# "Struck from the record" page. Nothing may ever be published at /nowhere.
#
# 302 (temporary) on purpose. These lines are a decision, not a law of
# physics; a 301 would sit in browsers' caches long after a line was removed,
# and the site would look broken rather than changed.
#
# The same list lives in DENY_PATHS in tools/repo_checks.py, which fails the
# build if any address here loses its rule. tools/check_live.py proves the
# rules are really live, against the deployed site, after a deploy.

# Curation and review sheets. audit/review.html also fetches and renders an
# arbitrary ?src= URL, so being unreachable is its fix as well as its cover.
/audit/*              /nowhere  302

# Python tooling, the compiler's config, the test suite, retired code.
/tools/*              /nowhere  302
/tests/*              /nowhere  302
/attic/*              /nowhere  302
/design-reviews/*     /nowhere  302

# Working documents: plans, rulings, checklists, content inventories.
/CRITIC_REPORT.md     /nowhere  302
/HOUSE_RULES.md       /nowhere  302
/LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md  /nowhere  302
/PLAN.md              /nowhere  302
/README.md            /nowhere  302
/connections_audit.md /nowhere  302
/content-inventory.md /nowhere  302

# Repository machinery that Pages uploads along with everything else.
/.github/*            /nowhere  302
/.claude/*            /nowhere  302
